--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,36 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Sign in with an existing reader account and open **Account settings** in the header.
+Readers can register a passkey, see its creation and last-used dates, rename it, or
+remove it. Registration and passkey sign-in verify the browser response, origin,
+RP ID, user verification, and a short-lived session challenge on the server.
+Password sign-in remains available after removing the last passkey.
+
+Use Node.js 22.18 or later. Passkey records are stored in SQLite at
+`data/passkeys.sqlite` by default. Set `PASSKEY_DATABASE_PATH` to a file on a
+persistent, writable volume in deployment; back up this database along with its
+WAL files. Use one Node deployment with this database, or replace the store with
+a shared database before running multiple instances. Astro's filesystem session
+storage also needs persistent storage (or a shared session driver for multiple
+instances). Existing password authentication still uses the configured Times
+login service; passwords and its tokens are not stored in the passkey database.
+
+Passkeys require HTTPS (localhost is supported for development). The RP ID defaults
+to the request hostname; `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` can pin it to your stable production
+domain. Changing the RP ID makes existing passkeys unusable on the new domain.
+
+After loading or changing the authoritative passkey list, supported browsers are
+notified through `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials`. Failed or
+unsupported sync shows manual password-manager cleanup guidance and a retry.
+Unrecognized credentials during passkey sign-in use `signalUnknownCredential`
+when available. Display names are per-key labels in the Times settings; WebAuthn
+has no API for renaming an individual key in a password manager. Account identity
+names are deliberately kept separate from these labels.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for storage isolation and browser-sync tests, `pnpm build` for the
+production build, and `pnpm check` for Astro/TypeScript diagnostics. The repository
+currently has existing type errors in the article/image/navigation code.
